+### TASK-066: the invisible-character check refuses by category (2026-11-17, one builder round)
+- **The increment.** R-086 (J1, ISS-031): `invisible-check.py` decides by the Unicode category, read from `unicodedata`, in place of its list of named code points: every character of Cc, Cf, Zl and Zp, and of Zs other than U+0020, is a finding, but for U+0009, U+000A and U+000D anywhere and U+FEFF as the file's first character; a finding prints its Unicode name lower-cased as before, or ends at its code point where the character has none (every Cc character). Every character of the old list is in those categories with the same name, so no existing finding line changed; the options, the exits, what it reads, the `--non-ascii` listing and the `RESULT:` lines are byte-identical (Review A compared both programs over the same scratch repository). The reality check ruled the plan's "the staged files, or the paths given" as built: the files changed against a base plus the untracked ones, or every tracked file with `--all`; the pre-commit gate does not call the program, so the plan's clause on fixtures read through its paths had no object.
+- **The sweep (the supervisor's commit 5dcb572, before the checkpoint).** run/supervisor/sweep_066.py, R-086's rule read as the program reads, found 15 characters in 5 of 946 tracked files, each a typed escape that arrived as the character (KP-052): U+2028 and U+2029 in handoff/BUG-032-r3.md, TASK-031-r9.md and TASK-033-r3.md, beside the escape text they were meant as; U+FEFF, U+200B, U+202E and U+00AD in tests/test_invisible_check.py and U+00A0 and U+3000 in tests/test_workflow_check.py, each inside a normal string literal. Each was replaced by its backslash-u escape text, so no test's runtime value changed. After the builder's run the new program over the Workspace: `RESULT: OK - no invisible character in 946 file(s)`. No tracked path holds a character git quotes (checked with `ls-files -z`), so `--all` read every one of them (lead 1).
